{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"browny-fur-hyrax","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEmpty `file_impact` is overloaded (see parent epic): \"the author forgot\" and \"this ticket\nchanges no code\" are the same value today, so every consumer must assume the conservative\nreading. This story adds the missing third state to the data model and every surface that\nwrites or reads it. No gate behavior changes here — consumers are wired in S2/S3/S4/S5.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend the existing `FILE_IMPACT` event rather than adding a new event type, so the\nlast-writer-wins semantics already implemented in\n`process_file_impact` (src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:527) make the states inherently\nmutually exclusive: a later declaration replaces an earlier one, in one place.\n\nEvent payload gains two optional keys alongside `file_impact`:\n\n```json\n{\"file_impact\": [], \"code_impact\": \"none\", \"code_impact_reason\": \"docs-only: rewrites docs/x.md prose\"}\n```\n\nReducer state gains `code_impact` (default `\"undeclared\"`) and `code_impact_reason` (default\n`\"\"`). `process_file_impact` sets BOTH on every FILE_IMPACT event, so recording paths after a\n`none` declaration resets the state to `\"paths\"` with an empty reason, and vice versa. The\nderivation rule is fixed and single-sourced in one helper:\n\n- non-empty `file_impact` → `\"paths\"` (any `code_impact` in the payload is ignored);\n- empty `file_impact` + `code_impact == \"none\"` → `\"none\"`;\n- otherwise → `\"undeclared\"`.\n\nWrite surface — CLI keeps ONE verb (`set-file-impact`) with a new mutually-exclusive form:\n\n```\nrebar set-file-impact <id> '[{\"path\":\"…\",\"reason\":\"…\"}]'     # unchanged\nrebar set-file-impact <id> --none \"<reason>\"                  # new\n```\n\n`--none` requires a reason of at least 10 non-whitespace characters (a bare `--none` or\n`--none \"\"` is a usage error, exit 2) — the reason is what the S4 criterion reviews. Passing\nboth a JSON array and `--none` is a usage error.\n\nRead surface — `get-file-impact` keeps its array shape (its schema is an array and\n`next_batch` consumes it); the tri-state is read through a new\n`rebar.get_code_impact(ticket_id) -> {\"kind\": str, \"reason\": str, \"paths\": list}` library\nfunction and is included in `show`/ticket-state output via the reducer state keys.\n\nMCP gets a dedicated write tool `declare_no_code_impact(ticket_id, reason)` rather than\noverloading `set_file_impact`'s array parameter, so each tool keeps a single clean\n`outputSchema`; `set_file_impact` is unchanged over the wire and still resets the state to\n`\"paths\"`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_state.py` — initial state keys `code_impact` / `code_impact_reason`.\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` — `process_file_impact` sets the tri-state; the\n  derivation helper lives here next to the processor that applies it.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py` — `set_file_impact` grows a `no_code_impact_reason` keyword;\n  reason-length validation.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/__init__.py` and `src/rebar/_cli/help/set-file-impact.txt` (created if\n  absent) — the `--none` argument form and its help text.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_gates.py` — `set_file_impact` passthrough plus `get_code_impact`.\n- `src/rebar/__init__.py` — export `get_code_impact` and `declare_no_code_impact`.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` — the `declare_no_code_impact` tool.\n- `src/rebar/schemas/common.schema.json`, `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json` — the\n  `code_impact` enum + `code_impact_reason`; `src/rebar/schemas/gen_types.py` regeneration\n  into `src/rebar/types.py` (`TicketState`).\n- `docs/event-schema.md` — the FILE_IMPACT event's new keys.\n\nOut of scope (later children): manifest/attestation behavior, container inheritance, the P9\nlint, the new review criterion, the close gate.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Reducer unit tests: each of the six transitions between the three states (including\n  paths→none→paths) lands the expected `code_impact` / `code_impact_reason` pair.\n- CLI tests: `--none \"<reason>\"` appends the event; `--none` with a short/empty reason exits\n  2 with a usage error; array + `--none` together exits 2.\n- Schema test: a state carrying `code_impact: \"none\"` validates against\n  `ticket_state.schema.json`, and an unknown `code_impact` value fails validation.\n- MCP test: `declare_no_code_impact` round-trips through the reducer state.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar set-file-impact <id> --none \"<reason ≥10 chars>\"` records the declaration, and\n      `rebar.get_code_impact(<id>)` returns `{\"kind\": \"none\", \"reason\": <reason>, \"paths\": []}`\n      (checked: CLI + library test).\n- [ ] Recording a non-empty JSON array after a `--none` declaration returns the ticket to\n      `{\"kind\": \"paths\", \"reason\": \"\"}` (checked: reducer transition test).\n- [ ] A ticket that has never been declared returns `{\"kind\": \"undeclared\", …}` and existing\n      `get-file-impact` output is byte-identical to before this change (checked: existing\n      `get-file-impact` tests pass unmodified).\n- [ ] `--none` with a reason under 10 non-whitespace characters exits 2 with a message naming\n      the minimum (checked: CLI test asserting exit code and message).\n- [ ] The MCP tool `declare_no_code_impact` is listed with an `outputSchema` and sets the same\n      state as the CLI (checked: MCP tool test).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the full test suite pass.","id":"1934-63dd-4be9-4c48","parent_id":"94d9-f225-844c-43e5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Tri-state code impact: FILE_IMPACT carries an explicit 'no code changes' declaration"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785196775745470001,"uuid":"724a7905-675d-4b3c-9841-8d89a66e5661"}